# First Barre: F (repertoire plan: st-barre-f). An original 16-bar chord study in C major:
# C (x32010) to the full F barre (133211) and back, two bars each, then Am (x02210) to F.
# Two half-note strums per bar. The second bar of every F is the check: pick the six strings one
# at a time, from string 6 to string 1, and listen for any that buzz or die, then use the rest to
# move to the next chord. The last bar checks once more and ends on a strum.
# F barre fingers: finger 1 flat across all six strings at fret 1, finger 2 on string 3 fret 2,
# finger 3 on string 5 fret 3, finger 4 on string 4 fret 3.
# On a bad day, play Fmaj7 (xx3210) wherever F appears: same root, no barre.
title: First Barre: F
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original chord study for Sixstring Academy
